## Context

Tracked by 0876 (audit before the neutral migration); this ticket is the
first removal it authorises, and does not close it.

First cut of the pre-port slimming. A usage census over every local session
trace (5 680 files, 3,42 GB, all repositories) found eleven skills with zero
invocations in the measured window. The author selected four of them for
removal now; the editorial-lifecycle group (ingest-decision-letter, release,
bib-merge, related-work-note-validate) is deferred to a separate discussion,
and related-work-note is kept because a live skill cites it.

Two independent measurements agree on the zero/non-zero split for all 37
skills, with no disagreement: this census, and `scripts/mammoth-audit.py` from
the sibling merge request (ticket 0876), run against the same corpus. The four
skills below carry zero active references in both.

Nothing outside their own directories and their own tests refers to them. The
only regenerated file is the `README.md` catalog.

Measured, for the record: each of the four has existed for at least three
months and was never invoked once, by the author or by another skill.

  maw-audit        created 2026-06-05, 15 commits, 93 217 B
  test-audit-llm   created 2026-06-06,  4 commits, 47 108 B
  scry             created 2026-05-14,  7 commits, 18 327 B
  smoke            created 2026-04-25,  4 commits,  1 177 B

## Relevant files

- `skills/maw-audit/` — mutation-testing audit, 6 files
- `skills/test-audit-llm/` — read-and-judge test audit, 6 files
- `skills/scry/` — multi-repo pre-flight check, 2 files
- `skills/smoke/` — agent environment self-check, 1 file
- `tests/test_maw_audit_skill.py`, `tests/test_test_audit_llm_skill.py`
- `README.md` — generated catalog, regenerated by `make skills-catalog`
- `tests/test_model_rightsizing.py` — its workflow-`.js` lens loses its subject
- `scripts/test-quality.py` — docstring names the two removed siblings

## Actions

1. Remove the four skill directories.
2. Remove the two tests whose subject disappears. `scry` and `smoke` have none.
3. Regenerate the catalog with `make skills-catalog`.
4. Remove the workflow-`.js` lens from `tests/test_model_rightsizing.py`.
   The two removed skills held the repository's only `.js` workflows, so lens 1
   and its JS lexer now scan an empty corpus. The file's own
   `test_corpus_is_non_empty` guard caught this and went red, which is the guard
   working. Relaxing that guard would reinstate the vacuous green it exists to
   prevent, so the lens goes with its subjects; history restores it alongside
   the first workflow skill that returns.

## Test

`make check-skills-drift` is the red step: it fails while `README.md` still
lists a skill that no longer exists on disk, and passes once the catalog is
regenerated. It therefore proves the catalog was not left stale.

## Verification

- [ ] No reference to the four names survives outside `docs/` and closed tickets
- [ ] `make check-skills-drift` passes
- [ ] `make check` passes
- [ ] `tickets/erg check tickets/` passes

## Invariants

- No live skill, script, hook or rule changes behaviour.
- `git revert` restores any skill removed here; nothing is lost.

## Residual

`scripts/test-quality.py` (34 835 B) loses its only consumer with `maw-audit`.
It survives because `tests/test_ruff.py` and `tests/test_test_quality.py` still
exercise it. Left in place deliberately: removing it is a separate decision,
not a consequence of this one.

## Exit criteria

- Four skills and two tests removed, catalog regenerated, full suite green.
